# LeetCode 11. Container With Most Water
# https://leetcode.com/problems/container-with-most-water/
#
# Approach: Two-pointer technique starting from both ends. At each step,
# calculate area using the shorter height (since that's the limiting side),
# track the max, then move the pointer at the shorter height inward, since
# moving the taller one can only shrink the width without any chance of
# increasing the limiting height. If heights are equal, moving either
# pointer works, the area is bound by that height regardless.
#

This is my intial solution

def maxArea(self, height):
        left, right = 0, len(height) - 1
        max_area = 0
        while left < right:
            area = min(height[left], height[right]) * (right - left)

            if area > max_area:
                max_area = area
                
            if height[left] < height[right]:
                left += 1
            elif height[left] > height[right]:
                right -= 1
            else:
                left += 1

        return max_area


A problem I ran into was I didnt have a case for when the heights were equal to each other. My thought at that time was what pointer should be moved and I just decided on the left one since if it works it will work. Later, 
after checking my answer I learned it didnt matter what pointer was moved.
